From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: crossystem says nothing about the ChromeOS ACPI
 device on PCs

crossystem reads Chromebook firmware values from the ChromeOS ACPI device
(GOOG0016, or the older chromeos_acpi/GGL0001), which PCs don't have. It
looks for the device on every property (VbSharedDataVersion reads VDAT for
each one) and printed "ERROR: GetAcpiSysfsPath: Failed to get ChromeOS
ACPI sysfs path VDAT" each time: crosh opened with three such lines on
every NickelOS PC (it asks crossystem for cros_debug). The values are
simply not available there, which the callers already handle.

---
--- a/vboot_reference/host/arch/x86/lib/crossystem_arch.c
+++ b/vboot_reference/host/arch/x86/lib/crossystem_arch.c
@@ -128,9 +128,10 @@
 	else if (stat(current_path, &fs) == 0 && S_ISDIR(fs.st_mode))
 		ret = asprintf(&path, "%s/%s", current_path, name);
 
-	if (ret == -1)
-		fprintf(stderr, "ERROR: %s: Failed to get ChromeOS ACPI sysfs path %s\n",
-			__func__, name);
+	/* NickelOS: no message when the ChromeOS ACPI device isn't there, as
+	 * on every PC that isn't a Chromebook: crossystem looks for it on each
+	 * property, so every lookup printed one or more of these (three lines
+	 * when crosh opened). Callers take NULL as "not available". */
 
 	return ret == -1 ? NULL : path;
 }
